    "lyrics": "# **Leaning Not Leaving**\n\n# **Leaning Not Leaving**\n\n\\[Intro | Powerful Piano and Deep Cello Duet | Attention Grabbing\\]\n\n\\[Verse 1 | intimate | rhythmic kick drum pulse | breathy alto\\]  \nI was praying for a shoreline  \nwhere the waves don\u2019t ever break.  \nLooking for a version of peace  \nthat didn't have a price or an ache.  \nBut the silence isn't safety  \nand the comfort isn't the goal.  \nThere\u2019s a friction in the waiting  \nthat\u2019s meant to make me whole.\n\n\\[Pre-Chorus | building string tension | heartbeat kick\\]  \nI\u2019m dropping the anchor I held in my hand,  \nTrading the weakness that I understand.  \nHe\u2019s working in the weight to perfect the design,  \nThis is the pressure that makes the diamond shine.\n\n\\[Chorus 1 | anthemic | big lift | soaring strings | layered voices\\]  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nThere is a purpose in the pain,  \nA steady hand inside the flame\\!  \nI surrender the battle, I surrender the fight,  \nI trust the Father to turn on the light\\!  \nOh, it\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nYeah, it\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!\n\n\\[Verse 2 | driving kick drum | rhythmic strings\\]  \nI\u2019m done with the heavy lifting  \nof trying to save my own life.  \nI dropped the rope that held the knife,  \nI chose to surrender the strife.  \nIt cuts through the self-sufficient  \nit bleeds out the pride I\u2019ve known  \nUntil the only comfort I\u2019m left with...  \n\\[Power Belt | emotional climax\\]  \nIS CHRIST AND CHRIST ALONE\\!\n\n\\[Bridge | climax | massive vocal stack | heavy cinematic strings\\]  \nUnity is born when the pride starts to break\\!  \nPeace is the treasure that the fire can\u2019t take\\!  \nWe don\u2019t find the light by avoiding the dark  \nBut by letting the friction become the spark\\!  \nIt\u2019s the heart of the conflict where mercy is found,  \nOn the knees, in the heat, on this holy ground\\!\n\n\\[Chorus 3 | maximum intensity | cinematic choir\\]  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nThere is a purpose in the pain,  \nA steady hand inside the flame\\!  \nTrusting the Father, not the outcome,  \n\\[Power Belt\\]  \nUNTIL THE WORK IN ME IS DONE\\!\n\n\\[Outro | powerful multilayered vocals\\]  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving.  \nIt\u2019s the leaning... not the leaving.  \n\\[Intimate whisper | solo cello\\]  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving.  \nIt\u2019s the leaning... not the leaving.  \n\\[End\\]\n\n# **Leaning Not Leaving \\- Rock**\n\n# **Leaning Not Leaving \\- Rock**\n\n\\[Intro | Overdriven Marshall Stacks | Syncopated Snare Crack\\]\n\n\\[Verse 1 | Gritty Alto | Dry Vocals | Palm Muted Rhythm\\]  \nI was clawing for a shoreline  \nWhere the breakers never hit  \nBegging for a peace of mind  \nThat didn't cost a bit  \nBut the quiet isn't safety  \nAnd the ease is not the prize  \nThere\u2019s a friction in the waiting  \nOpening my eyes\n\n\\[Pre-Chorus | Rising Gain | Driving Kick\\]  \nI\u2019m cutting every anchor that I tried to hold  \nTrading in the copper for the Refiner\u2019s gold  \nHe\u2019s working in the pressure, grinding out the pride  \nTurning every shadow to a place I don't hide\n\n\\[Chorus | High Octane Rock | Staccato Chords | Layered Harmonies\\]  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nThere is a purpose in the fire  \nPulling me up higher  \nI surrender the ego, I surrender the fight  \nI trust the Architect to set the record right\\!  \nOh, it\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nYeah, it\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!\n\n\\[Verse 2 | Hard Driving | AC/DC Style Pocket\\]  \nI\u2019m done with the heavy lifting  \nOf playing my own God  \nI\u2019m walking off the stage now  \nAnd giving Him the nod  \nIt carves out the self-reliance  \nIt kills the hollow \"me\"  \nUntil the only rock I\u2019m standing on...  \n\\[Power Belt | Benatar Snarl\\]  \nIS CHRIST AND CALVARY\\!\n\n\\[Bridge | Climax | Solo Section | Heavy Riffage\\]  \nUnity is born when the ego starts to crack\\!  \nGrace is the weapon that the devil can't take back\\!  \nWe don\u2019t find the light by running from the dark  \nBut by letting the friction catch a Holy spark\\!  \nIt\u2019s the heart of the conflict where the blood is found  \nFace down in the dirt on this holy ground\\!\n\n\\[Chorus 3 | Maximum Stadium Energy\\]  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving\\!  \nThere is a purpose in the fire  \nPulling me up higher\\!  \nTrusting the Father, not the check in my hand  \n\\[Power Belt\\]  \nUNTIL I\u2019M STEADY IN THE PROMISED LAND\\!\n\n\\[Outro | Fading Riffs | Vocal Ad-libs\\]  \nIt\u2019s the leaning, not the leaving.  \nIt\u2019s the leaning... not the leaving.  \n\\[Raw Solo Guitar Feedback | Final Kick Hit\\]  \n\\[End\\]",
