    "lyrics": "# **Breath and Bone**\n\n# **Breath and Bone**\n\n\\[Verse 1: Crystal clear vocals\\]  \nThe iron was bolted  \nThe cedar was scarred  \nWe\u2019d walled out the world  \nEvery window was barred  \nWe were huddling in shadows  \nNursing our grief  \nLocked in a prison  \nOf pure unbelief  \nBut You didn\u2019t need permission  \nYou didn\u2019t need a key  \nYou didn\u2019t wait for a welcome  \nTo invade our misery  \nThrough the grain of the wood  \nThrough the weight of the stone  \nYou stood in our terror  \nAnd called us Your own  \nWe shivered like children  \nAt a ghost in the room  \nStartled by Life  \nBreaking out of the tomb\n\n\\[Chorus\\]  \nOh, behold the hands\\! Behold the feet\\!  \nWhere mercy and my wonder meet  \nYou\u2019re not a shadow, You\u2019re not a dream  \nYou\u2019re the breath and the bone of the King  \nMy heart is amazed  \nMy soul is undone  \nTouching the scars  \nOf the Living One  \nIt\u2019s really You\u2014not a ghost, but the Life  \nStanding here whole  \nThrough the death and the strife\n\n\\[Verse 2: Soft musical reset, intimate\\]  \n\"Why are you troubled?\"  \nYour voice hit the air  \nSilencing doubt  \nAnd the scent of despair  \nYou saw every \"questioning\"  \nRising within  \nThen offered Your side  \nAnd the price of our sin  \nWe were \"disbelieving for very joy\"  \nA hope that the darkness  \nCould never destroy  \nFrom the edge of the grave  \nTo the center of the room  \nThe Light of the World  \nHas emptied the gloom\n\n\\[Bridge: Drop instruments, Heavy marching snare drums enter\\]  \nYou asked for a seat  \nYou asked for a meal  \nTo prove that the scars  \nAnd the skin were both real  \nWe brought You the fish  \nFrom the coals of the fire  \nTo the God of the heavens  \nAnd the world\u2019s Great Desire  \nAnd as You were eating  \nThe doubts started fading  \nNo more \"disbelieving\"  \nNo more \"joy-filled waiting\"  \nThe Hands that held the stars  \nNow hold the common plate  \n\\[Crescendo: Bring up all instruments\\]  \nDeath has been conquered  \n\\[Big Vocal Belt\\]  \nAnd the stone has lost its weight\\!  \n\\[Final Chorus: Maximum volume, heavy marching drum emphasis\\]  \n(Chorus lyrics as above)  \n\\[Outro: Sudden drop to soft piano\\]  \nTouch and see...  \nFlesh and bone...  \nPeace be still...  \nYou're home.  \n\\[End\\]",
